{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EcscipaLZZUr2T7buCSXMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The round-robin approach gives much better balance:\n\n**Segment 1:** 93-100ms spread of 7ms (vs 83-109ms = 26ms before)\n**Segment 2:** 84-87ms spread of 3ms (vs 77-103ms = 26ms before)\n\nThis is dramatically improved. The spread went from 26ms to 7ms and 3ms respectively.\n\nNow let me check the critical-path improvement:\n- Before: slowest thread = 109ms (seg1), 103ms (seg2)\n\n\n- After round-robin: slowest thread = 100ms (seg1), 87ms (seg2)\n\nThat's 9ms improvement in seg1 and 16ms improvement in seg2, putting us right in the 15-30ms target range. Now I need to run proper benchmarks to get exact numbers, which means removing the debug logging overhead by disabling the tracing statements in release mode.\n\nActually, the `tracing::debug!` calls won't produce output at the default log level anyway, so they won't impact performance in the standard configuration. I'll keep them for diagnostics and run the full benchmark suite now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1040,"cache_read_input_tokens":60393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1040},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7d8193f-9a6a-449b-9cda-d3b0ae271652","uuid":"2627f10e-c49d-4c1a-8bf5-dc7a0e2a2173"}
